4. Decision for main to confirm, not blocking: exit 1 on a serve error. A permanent Accept error ends the session and kills the editor. "Temporary" is narrow: on Linux ENOBUFS/ENOMEM/EPERM/EPROTO from accept are not retried. On Windows any socket/AcceptEx failure except WSAECONNRESET/ERROR_NETNAME_DELETED is not retried either, WSAEMFILE/WSAENOBUFS included, because syscall.Errno.Temporary there compares against Go's invented EMFILE. It is loud, not silent, so I accept it as the worker's documented choice.
